# .clinerules
# Project Intelligence, Implementation Paths, Workflow Preferences, and Decisions

## Implementation Paths
- All core orchestrator logic and agent graph code is in `darchon/`.
- Features, onboarding, and architecture diagrams/specs are in `features/`.
- API documentation is in `api/`, deployment guides in `deployment/`.
- Custom tools/plugins go in `custom_tools/`.
- Docker build contexts for agents/tools are in `docker_repos/`.

## Workflow Preferences
- Always follow memory bank lifecycle and access patterns as defined in custom-instructions.md.
- Reference new custom/spec files in `activeContext.md` when added.
- Use standardized FastAPI wrappers and `/invoke` endpoints for all agent containers.
- Use docker-compose.yml as the single source of truth for agent/tool registration.

## Project-Specific Decisions
- Orchestrator platform is named `darchon`.
- Agent logic is loaded dynamically via environment variable `AGENT_GRAPH_PATH`.
- All agent-to-agent and orchestrator-to-agent communication is via HTTP/JSON on the Docker network `mcpnet`.
- Agent Conference Graph (LangGraph) is used for all-way agent communication and aggregation.

## Tool Usage Patterns
- Use memory bank structure for all documentation and context management.
- Update documentation in reverse-hierarchical order: progress → activeContext → others.
- Add integration guides and testing strategies as the project matures.

# End of .clinerules
